# Copy to `.env` and change what you need. Every value below is optional: with
# no .env at all this repo builds exactly as production does.
#
# Astro exposes `PUBLIC_*` variables to the CLIENT bundle as well as the build,
# which is what the blog shelf's browser-side refetch needs — so nothing in
# here may ever be a secret.

# ---- Origins (src/lib/site.ts) ---------------------------------------------

# This site's own public origin. Canonical / hreflang / Open Graph URLs.
# PUBLIC_URL=https://moddingcommunity.com

# website-city — the app. The landing page's blog shelf reads its public
# content API (`/api/content/article?official=1`), at build time and again from
# the browser once the baked pool is a day old. It is the UNAUTHENTICATED half,
# so a local city needs no key here.
# PUBLIC_CITY_URL=http://localhost:3000

# The documentation site (../website-learn). `/api-tool` links its CLI page at
# {PUBLIC_DOCS_URL}/tmc-cli.
# PUBLIC_DOCS_URL=https://docs.moddingcommunity.com

# ---- Page metadata (src/layouts/Layout.astro) -------------------------------

# PUBLIC_TITLE=The Modding Community
# PUBLIC_TITLE_MAIN=The Modding Community
# PUBLIC_FAV_ICON=/favicon.ico
# PUBLIC_SOCIAL_MEDIA_IMAGE=/images/banner.png

# ---- Analytics — both are off unless their script src is set ----------------

# Plausible
# PUBLIC_PA_SRC=https://plausible.example.com/js/script.js
# PUBLIC_PA_DOMAIN=moddingcommunity.com
# PUBLIC_PA_API=https://plausible.example.com/api/event

# Umami
# PUBLIC_UMAMI_SRC=https://umami.example.com/script.js
# PUBLIC_UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID=
